('All the Love Poems of Shakespeare', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/All_the_Love_Poems_of_Shakespeare-William_Shakespeare-d4a42-361965.jpg', 'William Shakespeare', 'Citadel', 'Foreign Language Books : Poetry', '9780806508559', 'English', 166, 'Edition, 1993', 2318.0, 2, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Measure For Measure', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Measure_For_Measure-William_Shakespeare-c1d12-350616.jpg', 'William Shakespeare', 'The Arden Shakespeare India', 'Foreign Language Books', '9789389812275', 'English', 440, '1st Edition, 2020', 700.0, 700, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Shakespeare''s Sonnets', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Shakespeares_Sonnets-William_Shakespeare-04cd3-339256.jpg', 'William Shakespeare', 'Bloomsbury Publishing (India)', 'Foreign Language Books : Poetry', '9789382563990', 'English', 512, '1st Edition, 2013', 798.0, 798, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Shakespeare''s Sonnets are universally loved and much-quoted throughout the world. First published in 1997 to much critical acclaim, the Sonnets has been a consistent best-seller in the Arden Shakespeare series. Katherine Duncan-Jones tackles the controversies and mysteries surrounding these beautiful poems head on, and explores the issues of sexuality to be found in them, making this a truly modern edition for today''s readers and students. This revised edition has been updated and corrected in the light of new scholarship and critical thinking since its first publication.'),
('Romeo and Juliet', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Romeo_and_Juliet-William_Shakespeare-64a47-338842.jpg', 'William Shakespeare', 'Wilco Publishing House (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: Drama', '9789390213214', 'English', 146, '1st Edition, 2020', 798.0, 798, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Romeo and Juliet WILLIAM SHAKESPEARE ‘What’s in a name? That which we call a rose By any other name would smell as sweet.’ A love story whose very mention has come to represent the height of romantic passion, Romeo and Juliet is amongst Shakespeare’s most well-known plays. Having been told across every format, language and platform, the book remains as popular as ever. In a world full of violence, hate and politics, love blossoms. But this love is ill-fated, because the two young lovers – Romeo and Juliet – come from warring families of the Montagues and the Capulets. Against all odds, the two must attempt to unite – but fate will decide whether that happens in life or in death.'),
('The Merry Wives of Windsor', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/imgrok_20141214_86333.gif', 'William Shakespeare', 'Penguin Publishing Group (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: Drama', '9780140714647', 'English', 160, '1st Edition, 2002', 1162.0, 1, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
