('The Plays of William Shakespeare, Vol. 17', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/The_Plays_of_William_Shakespeare_Vol_17-William_Shakespeare-be3f6-362125.jpg', 'William Shakespeare', 'Forgotten Books (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: Drama', '9781334051289', 'English', 644, 'Edition, 2018', 2824.0, 2, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Shakespeare in Love', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Shakespeare_in_Love-William_Shakespeare-e5b09-362016.png', 'William Shakespeare', 'Faber & Faber(India)', 'Foreign Language Books: Drama', '9780571200931', 'English', 73, 'Edition, 2000', 998.0, 998, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('The Oxford', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/The_Oxford-William_Shakespeare-c2f4d-361676.jpg', 'William Shakespeare', 'OUP Oxford University Press (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: Drama', '9780199535811', 'English', 416, 'Edition, 2017', 1198.0, 1, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('Romeo and Juliet', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Romeo_and_Juliet-William_Shakespeare-2d910-350193.jpg', 'William Shakespeare', 'The Arden Shakespeare India', 'Foreign Language Books: Drama', '9789382563228', 'English', 454, '1 January 2013', 700.0, 700, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', NULL),
('The Taming of The Shrew', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/The_Taming_of_The_Shrew_-William_Shakespeare-96501-547298.jpg', 'William Shakespeare', 'The Arden Shakespeare India', 'Foreign Language Books', '9789382563242', 'English', 468, 'Edition, 2013', 650.0, 650, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'The Taming of the Shrew is unique among Shakespeare''s plays and is a perennial and compelling success in the theatre. Its reception is marked, however, by ongoing polarised debate over the meaning and worth of the play. This edition disengages Shakespeare''s exuberant and disturbing marital farce from the tangled history of its reception. It views the two sixteenth-century Shrew plays as textually independent but theatrically interdependent and so includes the full text of The Taming of A Shrew in an appendix. While the Introduction and Commentary focus on the critical and theatrical debate surrounding the play, the original and comprehensive editing of the playtext makes available a ''different'' Shrew, more open to the reader''s interpretation than is usually the case. Barbara Hodgdon is a distinguished feminist scholar whose reading of the play offers a stimulating array of ideas and questions about this enduringly popular yet challenging comedy.'),
('Julius Caesar', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Julius_Caesar_-William_Shakespeare-ef534-563142.jpg', 'William Shakespeare', 'Harpercollins publishers (India)', 'Foreign Language Books', '9789373077758', 'English', 160, 'Edition , 2026', 498.0, 498, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', '''Friends, Romans, countrymen, lend me your ears.'' Returning victorious after a battle, General Julius Caesar is celebrated by the people of Rome. Jealous of his growing power and the fear of Caesar becoming the ruler, Cassius, a noble, conspires to assassinate him. Political chaos ensues as a consequence of ambition and betrayal. Based on true events from Roman history, Shakespeare''s Julius Caesar is the tragic play depicting a man''s personal dilemma over righteous action.'),
('Othello', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Othello_-William_Shakespeare-23919-563141.jpg', 'William Shakespeare', 'Harpercollins publishers (India)', 'Foreign Language Books', '9789373079172', 'English', 192, 'Edition , 2026', 398.0, 398, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', '''I am not what I am.'' Celebrated Moorish general Othello and Desdemona are bound by a secret love. When Othello is sent to war, his ensign Iago manipulates the truth to turn love into doubt and honor into ruin. Based on enduring themes of prejudice, betrayal and the destructive power of manipulation, Shakespeare''s Othello is a tragic study of unraveling trust and the cost of love in a jealous world.'),
('The Merchant of Venice', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/The_Merchant_of_Venice_-William_Shakespeare-a1ca9-566316.jpg', 'William Shakespeare', 'The Browser (India)', 'Foreign Language Books', '9789347590795', 'English', 128, 'Edition , 2026', 390.0, 390, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', '''To do a great right do a little wrong, And curb this cruel devil of his will.'' Some bargains are struck in desperation. Some are collected in rage. William Shakespeare''s The Merchant of Venice begins with one such bargain—Antonio, a merchant of Venice, borrows money from Shylock, a Jewish moneylender, to help his dear friend Bassanio court the wealthy Portia. Should he default, the price is a pound of flesh. When fortune turns and Shylock—humiliated, bereaved, and denied—comes to collect, Venice must decide what justice truly means. Woven through with romance, disguise, and wit, the play moves between laughter and cruelty with breathtaking ease. But it is Shylock who lingers, wronged as much as wronging, impossible to dismiss. Written between 1596 and 1598, The Merchant of Venice is Shakespeare at his most provocative, asking questions about prejudice, mercy, and the law that four centuries have yet to answer.'),
