('A Midsummer Night''s Dream: The Graphic Novel', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/181b5e814_210714.jpg', 'William Shakespeare', 'Classical Comics', NULL, '9781906332914', 'English', 144, 'Reprinted, 2019', 3300.0, 3, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'Shakespeare''s best-loved play, A Midsummer Night''s Dream endures as an obvious choice for outdoor theatre on a warm summer evening. The marriage of Theseus to Hippolyta serves as a backdrop to tangled loves, amateur dramatics, and an argument between the Fairy Queen and King, Titania and Oberon, with events spilling over from their Fairy Kingdom into the real world of the forest. The course of true love never did run smooth! Written in 1595-6, it was an early success for The Bard. Its appeal is easy to see, and it truly has stood the test of time, being regularly performed all over the world; and now this masterpiece from the greatest playwright of them all is brought to you as a full-colour adaptation, in quick modern English for a fast-paced read.'),
